  "opening": [
    "At dawn the city speaks in one voice. By decree, every resident must answer in Japanese.",
    "Mr. Kotoba's inspectors carry ledgers from door to door. Anyone who fails the inspection is condemned.",
    "The inspector passes your door. A clerk left one name off the list: yours.",
    "At the gate, a scrap of paper reads 水. You trace the four strokes. Water spills from the ink.",
    "Past the gate, the inspectors guard the animal district and the road through the storm.",
    "Their ledgers lead to Mr. Kotoba. You pocket the pen and set out for the first gate."
  ],
  "ending": [
    "Mr. Kotoba turns the last page. His own exam has been turned against him.",
    "His final seal cracks. Mr. Kotoba falls, and the examination hall opens.",
    "The gates unlock. Outside, the people gather to read the orders that kept them apart.",
    "They take the inspection notices down and put up a sign for a free class.",
    "A student asks how to write water. You draw 水, stroke by stroke, and pass them the pen.",
    "The city still has much to learn. This time, there is room to make a mistake."
  ]
